<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section><div class="wrap">
<article class="read">
  <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <p class="hand big nolead">everything you were going to email us about</p>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>What is CodeOrbit?</summary>
    <p>CodeOrbit is a directory for developers — a place to find useful tools, copy-ready code snippets, short video breakdowns, programming concepts explained through MemeLearn comics, and articles worth actually finishing.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Is CodeOrbit free to use?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Browsing tools, snippets, videos, MemeLearn and the blog is completely free, with no account required.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Do I need to sign up to use the site?</summary>
    <p>No. You can browse everything without creating an account. Signing in is only needed for the CodeOrbit team to manage content.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>How do I copy a code snippet?</summary>
    <p>Every snippet has a "Copy" button in its window header. Click it and the code is copied straight to your clipboard — no need to select the text manually.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>What is MemeLearn?</summary>
    <p>MemeLearn explains programming concepts through short comic-style panels, followed by a plain-language explanation underneath. It's built for the ideas that are usually explained with more jargon than they need.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Can I suggest a tool, snippet, or video to be added?</summary>
    <p>Yes — reach out through the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> with a link and a short note on why it's useful, and the CodeOrbit team will take a look.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>I found a bug or broken link. How do I report it?</summary>
    <p>Please use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> and include the page URL and what went wrong — the more detail, the faster it gets fixed.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Does CodeOrbit sell or share my personal data?</summary>
    <p>No. CodeOrbit does not sell personal information. See the full <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for details on what's collected and how it's used.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Can I reuse CodeOrbit's content elsewhere?</summary>
    <p>CodeOrbit's content, design and branding are protected under our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and license. You're welcome to link to CodeOrbit publicly, but reproducing or republishing content requires written permission.</p>
  </details>
</article>
</div></section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %> 